info.description:
\*_Test collection for the BAML PoC: one request per key BAML feature, called through FastAPI against the local model.__\*_

All requests are POST with a JSON body.

- /extract - structured output: turns free text into a typed ticket.  
    In: {"text": "Payment page crashes for all users since the 2.3 deploy."}  
    Out: {"title": "...", "priority": "LOW" | "MEDIUM" | "HIGH", "tags": \["..."\]}


- /stream - same as /extract, but streams partial tickets as the model writes (JSON Lines, one object per line; fields fill in progressively, the last line is the final ticket).  
    In: {"text": "Typo on the About page footer."}  
    Out: {"title": null, "priority": null, "tags": \[\]}  
    {"title": "Typo on the About page footer", "priority": "LOW", "tags": \["typo", "footer"\]}


- /classify - dynamic types: the categories you send are added to the enum at runtime; the model must pick one of them.  
    In: {"text": "My invoice charged me twice this month.", "categories": \["BILLING", "TECHNICAL", "SALES"\]}  
    Out: "BILLING"


- /client-registry - same ticket as /extract, but the LLM client is built in code at request time (here only temperature changes).  
    In: {"text": "Export to CSV is a bit slow.", "temperature": 0.2}  
    Out: {"title": "...", "priority": "...", "tags": \["..."\]}


- /collector - same ticket as /extract, plus the tokens used by that call.  
    In: {"text": "Dark mode resets after logout."}  
    Out: {"ticket": {...}, "input_tokens": 107, "output_tokens": 173}


- /checks - validation on an order. quantity has @assert (> 0): if it fails, the whole response is rejected (500). email has @check (contains "@"): the response always passes, and the check result is attached.  
    In: {"text": "Please send 3 boxes, contact me at [ana@example.com](https://mailto:ana@example.com)"}  
    Out: {"quantity": 3, "email": {"value": "[ana@example.com](https://mailto:ana@example.com)", "checks": {"has_at": {"status": "succeeded", ...}}}}


- /tools - the model picks one tool and fills in its arguments (nothing is executed). Note: the field is "request", not "text".  
    In: {"request": "What is the weather in Cluj?"}  
    Out: {"tool": "get_weather", "city": "Cluj"}  
    or {"tool": "send_email", "to": "...", "body": "..."}


If the model does not follow the schema (e.g. the text asks it to do something else), BAML raises a validation error and the API returns 500.  
Calls are sent automatically to Boundary Studio (traces).

body.raw:
{
    "text": "My invoice charged me twice this month.",
    "categories": [
        "BILLING",
        "TECHNICAL",
        "SALES"
    ]
}

{
    "text": "Export to CSV is a bit slow.",
    "temperature": 0.0
}

{
    "text": "Please send 3 boxes, contact me at ana@example.com"
}
